  speakerName: Kyros
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'Naimbag nga aldaw, traveler! Kalaw told me a new adventurer was
    exploring Vigan.

    When the morning has passed and the afternoon arrives,
    Ilocanos can greet someone by saying ''naimbag a malem.''

    It means ''good
    afternoon.''

    You can use it when greeting someone during the afternoon.

    Listen
    carefully: naimbag a malem.

    Now, try saying ''naimbag a malem'' yourself.'
